sRe the general thread about the value of patents in terms of rewarding 
people for their intellectual efforts--I have done a little thinking 
about one such idea--and have not done anything with it because I 
can't think of a way I could be rewarded for the idea.  I might as 
well go into details, because somebody who can think of a way to 
profit from it might be interested in a joint venture.  Posting to 
this private list should *not* be considered publishing the idea. 

Desalting sea water takes a pressure difference (depending on the 
brine concentration) of up to 3000 feet (in the 100 atomosphere 
range).  For near zero increases in brine concentration, as little as 
a 900 foot head might suffice.  If you have a deep enough trench 
handy, the three percent difference in density between fresh and salt 
water will give the required pressure, and you get fresh water for 
free.  (The energy comes from lowering salt into the depths.) 

California does not have deep enough water off the coast to make this 
process energy free, though it does cut the pumping cost some.  One 
possible implementation would be to put long pipes on the ocean bottom 
at right angle to the current in with large area surfaces sticking up 
into the current and draining into the pipes. 

But the *real* place to install this puppy is in Israel.  Put the 
collection area out where the water is about a mile deep, which 
supplies about 150 feet of head, pump it 750 feet up, out of the 
ocean, up over the mountains, and recover all of the of pumping energy 
(plus!) by letting *fresh* water flow through turbines to nearly the 
elevation of the Dead Sea (-13,000 feet).  Ignoring losses, one part 
in 13 flowing to the Dead Sea would recover all the pumping energy 
need to desalt sea water, with the rest providing all the irrigation 
water Israel (and for that matter Jordan) could ask for.  (Ok, three  
parts in 13 if you have to go to the 100 atomospheres used in regular 
reverse osmosis systems.) 

Anyone have an idea ("intellectual property") on how to profit from 
this piece of "intellectual property" which they would like to trade 
for a part interest in the one I have presented here?  I am not much 
interested in trying to patent this in Israel unless someone wants to 
put up the money.  This is just too subject to expropriation. 

